00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:54.950
Banks were born to help
us manage our money.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:57.620
Over the years, the value
provided by the bank

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:01.670
has expanded from checking,
savings, and personal loans,

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:05.840
with money transfer solutions
and bill pays and rewards.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:10.460
Sadly, these solutions feel
disconnected even today.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.350
It is time for a
simpler experience

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:15.080
with deeper integrations
into the bank

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.570
and each aspect
of our lives so we

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:20.630
don't have to carry so many
different apps on our phones

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:24.670
for utility, credit cards,
and to manage our budget.

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:27.610
Another example is it
is a common practice

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.190
for hotels and airlines
to leverage banks

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.200
to create their
own credit cards.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.930
We should see a future
where more services can

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:38.530
be offered via banking
as a service model, which

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:42.190
is modular, cloud-native
digital bank architecture that

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:45.640
offers financial products
and services via APIs

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.170
and microservices.

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:48.490
Why modular?

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:52.660
Well, because value-added
services on digital platforms

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:56.980
enable the bank to quickly adapt
to emerging markets and demands

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.140
by measuring
success and outcomes

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:03.520
and can allow them to build new
products in a matter of days

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.280
and not months or years.

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.470
Now, another example
here is banks

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:11.620
are able to easily provide
e-commerce retailers

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:15.010
with a value-added service
that offers instant loans

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:19.090
or buy now, pay later checkout
options on their websites.

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:21.190
And the only way
this is possible

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:24.410
is with a modular architecture.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:28.720
So now that we know that we
need a modular architecture,

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:31.120
let's see what it
takes to get there.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.950
Here are some of
the API products

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.710
that are central to
embedded finance, which

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:38.620
refers to core banking
services, which

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:42.160
includes opening an account
or checking balance and making

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.060
payments.

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:46.030
But managing these API
products and services

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:49.390
has increased in scale,
cost, and complexity

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:53.290
because the legacy architecture
was a one-on-one mapping

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:56.620
between core banking system
and the banking front end,

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.480
such as the website.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.820
The modern banking
as a service model

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:05.410
requires one-to-many mapping of
the core banking microservices

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:07.090
with an API layer.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:10.480
This new platform enables
business transformation

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.380
by embedding and integrating
core capabilities securely

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:17.690
with as many new systems
and partners as needed,

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:22.520
such as airlines, utilities,
transportations, and telcos.

