00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:38.050
So now that we know
what problem you're

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:41.270
solving when it comes to
modernizing retail banking,

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:43.570
let's see how we solve it--

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:47.470
time to dive into the high-level
components that we need.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:51.850
A modern digital bank comprises
of multiple business functions

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:53.180
and capabilities.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.840
These logical components
can be organized

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.210
into a few high-level
categories.

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:01.390
Let's consider a fictitious
financial institution,

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:02.740
Symbol Bank.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:05.890
It has to have services
across various channels

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:08.020
to serve the external customers.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:10.690
These could include
applications that directly

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:13.610
serve the customers-- the
payments, the operation

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:17.290
services for onboarding,
management, servicing, and then

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.940
the partner services.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:21.190
Then comes the
integration services,

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.590
which act as the
interoperability and

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:26.200
connectivity layer for
all the bank's services

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.580
and applications--

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.980
essentially, the
technology glue that

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:33.910
brings the core platform
data and various applications

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:36.970
together to orchestrate
and provide a business

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:39.520
function for the
bank to its users.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:42.610
Then there are the data
applications and platform,

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:45.940
which include the various
data pipelines-- streaming,

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:48.760
processing, governance,
and data warehousing

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:51.010
for applications and services.

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:53.230
The enterprise
application services

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:56.170
make up the enterprise
back office services

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:59.440
that keep the business
operating and compliant.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:02.440
Well, these include various
foundational components

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:06.700
of the bank, like finance
and treasury, financial ERP,

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.250
the governance,
risk, and control,

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:12.770
the regulatory reporting,
and audit and compliance.

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:16.750
Now, core application services
are those core services

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.900
and applications and data
that are required for a bank

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:23.710
to offer products and
services to their customers.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:26.290
These include the
core banking data

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:30.370
models for sensitive customer
information, transactions,

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:34.300
products, and things like that
as well as all the processing

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:37.100
and persistence of that data.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:40.660
Now, additional core services
include card management,

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:44.680
payments, collections, and
credit and fraud risks.

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:47.410
Then there are the
infrastructure operations

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:51.280
and security components that
apply to all functional aspects

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.090
of the bank's capabilities.

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:55.540
These are considered
foundational components

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:59.380
to ensure the bank's customer
data, integrity, and privacy

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:02.470
with appropriate
controls and policies

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:05.110
that adhere to the
bank's internal controls

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:06.850
and government regulations.

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:09.730
Now that we know what
capabilities a bank

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:12.250
needs or offers, we
are ready to dive

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:14.890
into the architecture
to make this work.

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:16.690
Well, in this part
of the video, we

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:20.440
are going to look at each of the
segments of the retail banking,

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:25.030
one by one, from channel
services, integration services,

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:29.260
data applications and platforms,
enterprise application

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:34.030
services, core application
services, and infrastructure,

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:37.140
security, and operations.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:40.710
Channel services include
services for customer channels,

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:43.320
such as banking and
customer services,

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:46.650
using Contact Center
AI and messaging.

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:50.370
Transaction channels, such
as credit and debit payments

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:53.370
using Google Pay,
and partner channels,

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:55.410
which is connecting
with open banking

00:06:55.410 --> 00:07:00.120
APIs and other marketplaces
using Apigee API Gateway--

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:03.060
now, these services power
the customer applications,

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:06.510
such as the ones needed
for operations, onboarding,

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:08.790
management, servicing
the customer,

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:12.630
showing customers the right
ads, sales, marketing,

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:15.100
and loyalty apps.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.050
Then you have the
integration layer,

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:20.640
which comprises the API
connectors on Apigee API

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:21.540
Management.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:24.850
These connectors take
the real-time and batch

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:27.600
unstructured and structured
data and then pass it

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:30.780
on to the data science
layer for further analysis

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:35.040
and creating unique user
experiences, like personalized

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:37.530
recommendations and
propensity models,

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:41.790
or preventing financial
crime with fraud prediction

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:45.270
and anomaly detection
with Vertex AI platform.

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:47.580
You can also run
high-performance computing

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:52.800
workloads using Tensor
GPUs within Vertex AI.

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:56.250
In addition, Vertex AI
streamlines the IML pipelines

00:07:56.250 --> 00:08:00.780
and provides explainable AI
outputs and model governance.

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:02.550
Now, Event and
Transformation Hub

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:06.450
also ingests the batch
data through Cloud Storage

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:09.750
and real-time data through
Pub/Sub messaging service

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:13.110
and passes it on to data
flow for transformation

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:15.000
and orchestration.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:19.590
The processed data is then sent
to serverless data warehouse,

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:23.640
BigQuery, and metadata that is
stored in Cloud Storage, which

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:25.080
is a data lake.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:27.660
Other teams and
applications can then

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:30.720
access this data through
a unified data management

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:33.240
catalog, Dataplex.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:35.280
As you can see,
the data platform

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:38.340
enables the bank to
securely process and store

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:42.900
sensitive customer data while
enriching with additional data

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:44.940
sets to gain a
better understanding

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:47.880
of their customers and products.

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:50.970
Then comes the enterprise
application services

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:53.460
that make up the
back office services,

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:56.850
which keep the business
operating and compliant.

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:59.520
And these include various
foundational components

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:04.050
of the bank, like finance
and treasury, financial ERP,

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:08.640
visualizations, regulatory
reporting, audits, compliance,

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:10.950
governance, risk, and control.

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:13.500
We query the data of
a BigQuery and then

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:17.700
use it to generate
visualizations in Looker.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:20.460
Core application services
are the core services

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:23.820
that are required for a
bank to offer its products

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:25.740
and services to the customers.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:27.240
Now, these services
are typically

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:30.750
deployed as microservices
on Kubernetes Engine

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:35.410
with transaction, products, and
customer data on Cloud Spanner.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:38.790
Event-driven microservices
communicate with each other

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:41.250
using Cloud Pub/Sub.

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:45.420
Additional core services
include card management

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:49.440
and payments and collections
and credit and fraud risk.

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:53.250
Then there are the core security
and operational components

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:56.130
that apply to all the
functional aspects of the bank's

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:57.150
capabilities.

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:00.630
Now, these services include
identity and access management

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:04.200
for authentication and
authorization standards, data

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:09.030
locality, encryption and key
management, data anonymization

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:12.720
and tokenization, along
with system, network,

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:17.220
and application logs for access
transparency and monitoring

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:19.320
incidents and SLAs.

